.po 1i
.TH HISTORY 1C UCB
.V 08/15/84 16:54:26
.\"@[$]history.1C	1.5	08/15/84 16:54:26 - Zilog Inc.
.ad
.fi
.SH NAME
history \- print list of previous commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhistory\fR
.br
\fBset history=\fIN\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commands input from the teminal are numbered sequentially from one and
are saved on the history list, whose size is controlled by the history
variable.
.PP
The contents of the history list is seen with the command:
.sp
.RS
\fBhistory
.RE
.PP
The size of the history list is determined by setting
the \fIhistory\fR shell variable with the command:
.sp
.RS
\fBset history=\fIN\fR
.RE
.sp
where \fIN\fR is the desired size of the history list
(15 is a recommended number).
.PP
These saved commands (also called events) are referred to
in the following ways:
.RS
.IP !n 12
event number n
.IP !-m 12
the desired even is m events prior to the current event
.IP !p 12
prefix of a command in an event
.IP !?string? 12
string in an event argument; trailing ? can be omitted if nothing
follows
.IP !! 12
immediately previous event
.RE
.PP
A history reference can be given without an event specification;
for example, !$.
In this case, the reference is to the previous command unless a previous
history reference occurred on the same line in which case this form
repeats the previous reference.
.SH SEE ALSO
set(1C), setenv(1C).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual

